			},
			"allod/suslanger": {
				"kind": "allod",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "Suslanger is a small, arid possession of Khadagan. Irrigation supports its farms, while harsh and corrupt authority coexists with criminal networks, smuggling and blackmail. Kir and Kel meet in its slave pen. Their escape leads through estates, thieves’ contacts, the Last Shelter and the search for information about the Joons before military papers provide a way to Gipath.",
						"sources": [
							"allod suslanger",
							"briefing brief_2",
							"briefing brief_41",
							"briefing brief_88a"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "allod suslanger",
				"id": "suslanger"
			},
			"allod/gipat": {
				"kind": "allod",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "Gipath remains outside the great empires and is strewn with Joon ruins. Lost in Astral presents a changed island after Zak’s journey: human expansion in the Foothills collides with the orcs, while the Free Hunters pursue their own interests. Kir and Kel must negotiate these disputes and recover the use of the Magic Orb before Tka-Rik can direct them onward.",
						"sources": [
							"allod gipat2",
							"briefing brief_112",
							"briefing brief_121",
							"briefing brief_137",
							"briefing brief_149"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "allod gipat2",
				"id": "gipat"
			},
			"allod/ingos": {
				"kind": "allod",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "Ingos is nominally Canian, but its governor’s effective power scarcely extends beyond the city walls. Independent communities and Woodsfolk inhabit the surrounding snowlands. Kir and Kel arrive following the Magic Orb’s clue. Brissen’s murder, a staged caravan and conflicting alibis make their visit an investigation; the cleared magician Yam-Akara discovers the route to Jigran.",
						"sources": [
							"allod ingos",
							"briefing brief_149",
							"briefing brief_245a",
							"briefing brief_250a",
							"briefing brief_251"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "allod ingos",
				"id": "ingos"
			},
			"allod/jigran": {
				"kind": "allod",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "Jigran is Kir’s homeland, a closed allod caught in perpetual autumn and war between Canian and Khadaganian forces. Firez’s necromancy has drained its fields and forests; much of the population shelters in fortified towns while undead roam outside. Kir returns through an old passage with Kel, joins the struggle led by Baron Virril and discovers the fate of the Joons he left behind.",
						"sources": [
							"allod jigran",
							"briefing brief_254",
							"briefing brief_304",
							"briefing brief_341",
							"briefing brief_349"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "allod jigran",
				"id": "jigran"
			},
			"map/bz1r": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "The recruiter’s camp offers Kir an apparent route to work beyond his homeland. Papers and a portal promise a new beginning; arrival on Suslanger instead delivers him into imperial captivity.",
						"sources": [
							"zone bz1r",
							"briefing brief_0",
							"briefing brief_1"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone bz1r",
				"id": "bz1r"
			},
			"map/bz1h": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "The slave pen is where Kir and Kel first form their partnership. Kel helps the beaten newcomer, while the officials reduce the prisoners to labour assignments. Their conversations turn captivity into the starting point of an escape.",
						"sources": [
							"zone bz1h",
							"briefing brief_2",
							"briefing brief_3b"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone bz1h",
				"id": "bz1h"
			},
			"map/bz2h": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "Rindeil’s mansion provides temporary shelter among an eccentric collector’s spiders. Karim offers gossip and useful contacts. The safety is conditional: when imperial searches threaten the estate, Rindeil withdraws his welcome.",
						"sources": [
							"zone bz2h",
							"briefing brief_6",
							"briefing brief_8",
							"briefing brief_40"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone bz2h",
				"id": "bz2h"
			},
			"map/bz3h": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "The Last Shelter is the fugitive brotherhood’s hidden refuge. Aliya brings Kir and Kel here, but Khatul tests them before granting trust. The smith’s change of attitude after acceptance makes membership a tangible part of life in the community.",
						"sources": [
							"zone bz3h",
							"briefing brief_41",
							"briefing brief_43",
							"briefing brief_43a",
							"briefing brief_45"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone bz3h",
				"id": "bz3h"
			},
			"map/bz4h": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "The Wormface temple gives Kir access to a people who recognise his Joon ancestry. The Brainripper invokes an ancient compact, but information and access still require action on the travellers’ part.",
						"sources": [
							"zone bz4h",
							"briefing brief_51",
							"briefing brief_52",
							"briefing brief_71"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone bz4h",
				"id": "bz4h"
			},
			"map/bz5h": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "The black market brings together craftspeople, illicit trade and local information. Master Arkhar and the fortune-teller offer very different services here. For conspicuous fugitives such as Kir and Kel, useful contacts are as valuable as equipment.",
						"sources": [
							"zone bz5h",
							"briefing nsheriff_about",
							"briefing skelet_about"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone bz5h",
				"id": "bz5h"
			},
			"map/bz8g": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "Urk-Tar’s fortress is the centre of Kir’s dealings with the orcs. The chief and shaman connect his arrival with memories of Zak, while ritual obligations, a kidnapped wife and conflict with human settlers make the stronghold a place of competing demands.",
						"sources": [
							"zone bz8g",
							"briefing brief_101",
							"briefing brief_102",
							"briefing brief_110",
							"briefing brief_112"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone bz8g",
				"id": "bz8g"
			},
			"map/bz11g": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "The Free Hunters’ camp is led by Bor. It gives Kir a foothold among people who claim independence from the village, yet intervene in its conflicts. Babur’s arrival through a deceptive message exposes how readily the camp’s interests become personal schemes.",
						"sources": [
							"zone bz11g",
							"briefing brief_121",
							"briefing brief_126a",
							"briefing brief_126b"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone bz11g",
				"id": "bz11g"
			},
			"map/bz12g": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "Estera’s cave remains a source of magical knowledge after Zak’s journey. Airy guards it in the witch’s absence. The visitors’ search for the Magic Orb becomes entangled with Estera’s flower, the Old Dragon and the two women’s disagreements.",
						"sources": [
							"zone bz12g",
							"briefing brief_129",
							"briefing brief_133",
							"briefing brief_136",
							"briefing brief_137"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone bz12g",
				"id": "bz12g"
			},
			"map/bz13g": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "The Dragon’s dwelling is another surviving landmark from Zak’s travels. The Old Dragon remembers the former Chosen but is currently more troubled by Estera’s demands about a flower. Kir and Kel must approach him through conversation and negotiation.",
						"sources": [
							"zone bz13g",
							"briefing brief_132",
							"briefing brief_133"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone bz13g",
				"id": "bz13g"
			},
			"map/bz14g": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "Tka-Rik’s underground home links the two campaigns. He explains that Zak and Lu-a-Jalla have left to travel, listens to Kir’s account of Jigran and interprets the Magic Orb. The resulting clue directs Kir and Kel to Ingos.",
						"sources": [
							"zone bz14g",
							"briefing brief_118",
							"briefing brief_119",
							"briefing brief_149"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone bz14g",
				"id": "bz14g"
			},
			"map/bz21k": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "The city of Ingos houses the governor, his court magician and the merchant Karansul. Their interests intersect with the murder inquiry: private relationships, a stolen nugget and the court’s own schemes all become relevant evidence.",
						"sources": [
							"zone bz21k",
							"briefing brief_201",
							"briefing brief_224",
							"briefing brief_245a",
							"briefing brief_247",
							"briefing brief_250a"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone bz21k",
				"id": "bz21k"
			},
			"map/bz22k": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "The Beastmasters’ settlement brings together Geraldine, Crooked, Trickster and Yam-Akara. Suspicion after the empty caravan tests the newcomers’ reception. The truth about Brissen’s death ultimately exposes a crime within this community.",
						"sources": [
							"zone bz22k",
							"briefing brief_212",
							"briefing brief_215",
							"briefing brief_250a"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone bz22k",
				"id": "bz22k"
			},
			"map/bz23k": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "The Green Clan’s new home preserves the Woodsfolk presence on Ingos. Grey Leaf supplies memories of Brissen and clues for the investigation, while elder Khabburu’s requests express a concern for freedom extending even to captive animals.",
						"sources": [
							"zone bz23k",
							"briefing brief_207",
							"briefing fq15"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone bz23k",
				"id": "bz23k"
			},
			"map/bz31j": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "Dar-Leanos is the Canian stronghold where Kir meets Baron Virril, his son Dartas and Master Stark. Losses in the war and recurring undead attacks shape its needs. The city becomes the base for the struggle to reach Firez and free Jigran.",
						"sources": [
							"zone bz31j",
							"briefing brief_302",
							"briefing brief_303",
							"briefing brief_304"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone bz31j",
				"id": "bz31j"
			},
			"map/bz32j": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "This meeting place belongs to Uncle Rad, the sweets seller who secretly serves the baron. A password from Stark opens a channel for intelligence and practical help, including the search for powerful allies outside the cities.",
						"sources": [
							"zone bz32j",
							"briefing brief_305",
							"briefing brief_344",
							"briefing brief_348"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone bz32j",
				"id": "bz32j"
			},
			"map/cz1h": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "A brief respite on the escape route from Suslanger’s captivity. This is a transitional scene rather than an independent settlement; the connected locations show where the journey continues.",
						"sources": [
							"zone cz1h"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone cz1h",
				"id": "cz1h"
			},
			"map/cz2h": {
				"kind": "map",
				"sections": [
					{
						"heading": "Setting",
						"text": "The exit from the catacombs marks a transition between the underground escape route and the world outside. Its significance lies in the travellers’ progress through Suslanger, rather than a separate local community.",
						"sources": [
							"zone cz2h"
						]
					}
				],
				"name_key": "zone cz2h",
				"id": "cz2h"
			}
		}
	},
